# Camera recoil

For example, when you punch something with your fist, the screen shakes slightly on impact.

Below you can adjust the screen shake intensity (this option can also be changed later in "Options" -> "Accessibility").

<GuideCard>
  <GuideCVarSlider CVar="accessibility.screen_shake_intensity" Title="Screen shake intensity" Min="0" Max="1" Format="Percent" DisabledByCVar="accessibility.reduced_motion" Note="At 0%, the screen stays completely still during hits, gunfire, and explosions. Enabling 'Reduce motion of visual effects' also disables screen shake." DisabledNote="The slider is disabled because 'Reduce motion of visual effects' is currently enabled in Options."/>
</GuideCard>

<GuideCard Title="This is what it looks like (click to punch):">
  <GuideScreenShakePreview/>
</GuideCard>

<GuideCard Title="When screen shake triggers:">
  <GuideInfoItem Title="Melee strikes and incoming hits" Description="Punching or swinging a weapon slightly rocks the camera, while hits on your character cause a sharp screen jolt."/>
  <GuideInfoItem Title="Gunfire and explosions" Description="Firing weapons gives camera recoil, and nearby explosions make the screen noticeably shudder."/>
</GuideCard>
